    "durationMs": 250946,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified against the requirements.\n\n**Implementation** — `src/main.rs` (axum 0.8.4 + sqlx/PostgreSQL):\n- `POST /links` — validates via the `url` crate (absolute http/https with host, stored and returned exactly as submitted); custom codes are checked against 4–20 chars `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, auto-generated codes are 8 chars from the same alphabet with collision retry; duplicates return `409`\n- `GET /links/{code}` / `GET /r/{code}` — the redirect increments clicks atomically in a single `UPDATE ... RETURNING` statement, so it counts exactly once per request; `302` with the raw stored URL in `Location`\n- `GET /links` — list ordered by an identity column for guaranteed ascending creation order\n- A custom JSON extractor maps every body rejection (malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, invalid code) to `422` with an `error` field\n- Migrations (`migrations/0001_create_links.sql`) are applied programmatically at startup via `sqlx::migrate!`, before the listener binds; credentials come from `DATABASE_URL`\n\n**Verification** — exercised every endpoint with curl: creation (auto + custom codes), 409 duplicate, 422 for bad url/missing url/malformed JSON/short/long/illegal codes, boundary-valid 4- and 20-char codes, 302 Location headers (raw header equals stored URL), click counts, JSON 404s, and a full server restart confirming links and click counts persist in PostgreSQL.\n\n**Deliverables** — `start.sh` (runs the prebuilt release binary, foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`, builds only if missing) and a README with startup instructions. Release binary is already built, so `sh start.sh` comes up immediately."
  }
